{{- /*
  The Sources surface: what the outage indicator counts, every registered provider
  with its availability, and every collection gap opnview detected in the last day.

  THE OUTAGES COME FIRST, because the indicator in the bar opens this page and the
  reader who followed it came to see what it counted. One line per unit of the
  indicator's figure -- a kind with no healthy implementation, or one implementation
  the operator turned on that is not healthy -- and the named state at nought. The
  providers table then marks, in a column of its own, exactly the rows those outages
  are about: a row can be unavailable and count towards nothing (declined, or beside
  a healthy implementation of its kind), and installed-not-collecting or state
  unknown can count, so the availability mark alone could not say which rows the
  figure is made of.

  IT IS THE SERVER-RENDERED COUNTERPART OF THE SOURCE AVAILABILITY PRESET
  (docs/widget-catalogue.md). One row per provider row. Availability and
  activeness are two columns, because two implementations of one kind may both
  answer and opnview reads one of them; the operator's selection is a third,
  because a decision is not a probe result. The availability is a value of the
  preset's, with a square mark in its status colour beside a word in the ordinary
  text colour -- the step-3 mockup's treatment, where a status hue is a mark and
  never the text.

  THE DETAIL IS DATA, AND IT IS NEVER OFF SCREEN. It is a collector's own sentence,
  rendered verbatim, escaped and marked untranslated, and it is what a reader who
  followed a degraded widget here came for -- so it is not a column at the far
  right of a table wider than the page, where it was cut at desktop width with the
  scrollbar below the fold. Each provider's probe and detail sit on a line of their
  own directly under its row, the full width of the table, labelled, wrapping
  rather than truncating. The probe is data too: the endpoint that determined the
  row, as the collector recorded it, offered a line break after each slash so a
  path wraps between its components and never inside one. An instant is never
  broken inside itself.

  INSTALLED, NOT COLLECTING CARRIES THE OPNSENSE PAGE THAT TURNS IT ON, on the same
  line as the detail, under a label saying the change is made in OPNsense and never
  by opnview (docs/widget-catalogue.md, Source availability and Part 3). The link is
  the configured firewall URL and a path cited in opnsense_pages.go.

  THE GAPS ARE THE LAST 24 HOURS, newest first, and an empty list is a named state.
  The time a gap missed is spelled in days, hours, minutes and seconds.
*/ -}}
{{define "body" -}}
<h1>{{t "sources.title"}}</h1>

<section class="card" id="sources_outages" aria-labelledby="sources_outages_name">
<h2 id="sources_outages_name">{{t "sources.heading.outages"}}</h2>
{{- if .Outages}}
<ul class="outage-list">
{{- range .Outages}}
<li><span class="availability mark-bad">{{t .KindKey}}</span>{{with .ProviderKey}} <span class="outage-provider">{{t .}}</span>{{end}} <span class="outage-state">{{t .StateKey}}</span></li>
{{- end}}
</ul>
{{- else}}
<p class="empty-state">{{t "indicator.no_outage"}}</p>
{{- end}}
</section>

<section class="card" aria-labelledby="sources_providers">
<h2 id="sources_providers">{{t "sources.heading.providers"}}</h2>
<div class="table-frame">
<table class="data sources">
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.kind"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.provider"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.availability"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.outage"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.active"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "collection.label.selection"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.checked"}}</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Sources}}
<tr>
<td>{{t .KindKey}}</td>
<td>{{t .ProviderKey}}</td>
<td><span class="availability {{.Mark}}">{{t .Availability}}</span></td>
<td><span class="outage-flag{{if .InOutage}} counted{{end}}">{{t .OutageKey}}</span></td>
<td>{{t .ActiveKey}}</td>
<td>{{t .SelectionKey}}</td>
<td>{{if .CheckedState}}{{t .CheckedState}}{{else}}<span class="figure">{{.Checked}}</span>{{end}}</td>
</tr>
<tr class="diagnostic">
<td colspan="7">
<dl class="diagnostic">
<dt>{{t "sources.column.probe"}}</dt>
<dd class="probe">{{range $index, $part := .ProbeParts}}{{if $index}}<wbr>{{end}}<span class="datum" translate="no">{{$part}}</span>{{end}}</dd>
<dt>{{t "sources.column.detail"}}</dt>
<dd class="detail">{{if .DetailState}}{{t .DetailState}}{{else}}<span class="datum" translate="no">{{.Detail}}</span>{{end}}</dd>
{{- if .Pages}}
<dt>{{t "sources.label.opnsense_page"}}</dt>
<dd class="opnsense-pages">{{range $index, $page := .Pages}}{{if $index}} {{end}}<a class="opnsense-page" href="{{$page.URL}}" rel="noreferrer noopener">{{t $page.LabelKey}}</a>{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
</dl>
</td>
</tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section class="card" aria-labelledby="sources_gaps">
<h2 id="sources_gaps">{{t "sources.heading.gaps"}}</h2>
{{- if .RecentGaps}}
<div class="table-frame">
<table class="data">
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.kind"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.provider"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "collection.label.gap_reason"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.start"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "sources.column.end"}}</th><th scope="col">{{t "collection.label.missed_seconds"}}</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .RecentGaps}}
<tr>
<td>{{t .KindKey}}</td>
<td>{{t .ProviderKey}}</td>
<td>{{t .ReasonKey}}</td>
<td><span class="figure">{{.Start}}</span></td>
<td><span class="figure">{{.End}}</span></td>
<td>{{template "duration" .Missed}}</td>
</tr>
<tr class="diagnostic">
<td colspan="6">
<dl class="diagnostic">
<dt>{{t "sources.column.detail"}}</dt>
<dd class="detail">{{if .DetailState}}{{t .DetailState}}{{else}}<span class="datum" translate="no">{{.Detail}}</span>{{end}}</dd>
</dl>
</td>
</tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{- else}}
<p class="empty-state">{{t "state.source.no_recent_gap"}}</p>
{{- end}}
</section>
{{- end}}
